1
00:00:00,021 --> 00:00:01,815
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:06,213
In this lesson, we will set up voice
channels for team coordination.

3
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:10,539
Field teams need the correct channel
membership and working device audio

4
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:12,743
before an exercise or deployment.

5
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:16,605
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,606 --> 00:00:18,724
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,547 --> 00:00:23,480
A search team uses its team
channel during a training exercise.

8
00:00:23,706 --> 00:00:26,895
Coordinate field teams through
app-based voice channels.

9
00:00:27,122 --> 00:00:31,094
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

10
00:00:31,095 --> 00:00:33,549
scenarios, not default settings.

11
00:00:34,379 --> 00:00:36,831
Voice, Push-to-Talk voice channels.

12
00:00:37,058 --> 00:00:39,787
Create channels and add
the members who use them.

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,862
Availability also depends on PTT.

14
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,284
Check access in the target department.

15
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:51,086
Push-to-Talk, the Push-to-Talk add-on,
voice channels in the ResGrid apps.

16
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:54,748
Review seats, supported
clients and channel setup.

17
00:00:54,974 --> 00:00:59,939
PTT does not provide phone dispatch
alerts or certify radio replacement.

18
00:01:00,135 --> 00:01:02,997
Availability also depends on PTT.

19
00:01:03,159 --> 00:01:05,385
Check access in the target department.

20
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:09,084
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

21
00:01:09,301 --> 00:01:13,497
Step one, confirm Push-to-Talk
access and supported clients.

22
00:01:13,753 --> 00:01:17,846
Step two, create a training channel
and add its intended members.

23
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:22,519
Step three, join from two demo
devices and verify transmit,

24
00:01:22,654 --> 00:01:25,100
receive, and microphone permissions.

25
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:27,553
Now verify the result.

26
00:01:27,768 --> 00:01:32,378
Check membership and actual audio in
both directions on the devices used.

27
00:01:32,558 --> 00:01:35,679
Review channel access
after membership changes.

28
00:01:35,869 --> 00:01:37,866
A common problem to watch for.

29
00:01:38,027 --> 00:01:41,419
Push-to-Talk channel setup is
separate from phone voice alerts

30
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:43,466
and audio stream configuration.

31
00:01:44,274 --> 00:01:46,092
Your practice task is simple.

32
00:01:46,253 --> 00:01:49,298
Run a two-device training
channel check and record which

33
00:01:49,312 --> 00:01:51,333
members can transmit and receive.

34
00:01:51,512 --> 00:01:56,023
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

35
00:01:56,167 --> 00:02:00,128
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
